Hi SEM family,

I’m wondering if anyone has experience using SEM with population- or regional-level data that is routinely collected rather than experimentally derived.

Our project aims to explore the relationship between community-related factors and mental health outcomes. We’re currently developing a CFA model with three to four latent constructs (urbanity, community cohesion, community safety, and ethnic diversity).

With some modifications, our goodness-of-fit indices remain below acceptable thresholds, although the model requires numerous correlations that are theoretically supported. We are able to get a better-fitting model, but the observed variables included in our latent construct are less rich and more simplistic.

Has anyone worked with this type of data, and are there examples of published studies where goodness-of-fit measures were somewhat suboptimal but still considered acceptable in context?

Best wishes, Luke

